1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--the-pillars-of-language-learning","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/the-pillars-of-language-learning","sourceHash":"48b6634adbe71366bd3e51f925a28983af1aa547a6bc422e043feae8cd273ec8","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:12.077Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"The Pillars of Language Learning","zh":"语言学习的支柱"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The Refold method organizes all language learning activities into three pillars: <strong>Priming</strong>, <strong>Interactive Immersion</strong>, and <strong>Freeflow Immersion</strong>. Every activity you do falls into one of these categories, and a balanced approach across all three is what drives acquisition.","zh":"Refold 方法将所有语言学习活动分为三大支柱：<strong>预备学习</strong>、<strong>互动式沉浸</strong>和<strong>自由流沉浸</strong>。你进行的每项活动都属于其中一类，而兼顾这三者的均衡方法正是推动语言习得的关键。"}},{"id":"priming","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Priming","zh":"预备学习"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Priming is any activity where you're explicitly studying or preparing your brain to recognize something in immersion. The key idea: priming doesn't teach you the language. It <em>prepares</em> you to learn it when you encounter it naturally.","zh":"预备学习是指任何明确学习某项内容，或让大脑做好准备、以便在沉浸中识别它的活动。核心理念是：预备学习本身不会教会你这门语言，而是让你做好<em>准备</em>，以便在自然遇到语言时习得它。"}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Examples of priming activities: vocab study with Anki or other SRS tools, grammar study, sound study, ear training.</strong>","zh":"<strong>预备学习活动示例：使用 Anki 或其他 SRS 工具学习词汇、学习语法、学习语音、进行听辨训练。</strong>"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<a href=\"https://refold.la/learning-libraries?libraryType=activities&amp;pillar=Priming\">-&gt; See tutorials for all Priming activities</a>","zh":"<a href=\"https://refold.la/learning-libraries?libraryType=activities&amp;pillar=Priming\">-&gt; 查看所有预备学习活动的教程</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Priming is most effective in short, focused sessions. 10-20 minutes of vocab study is enough — more than that and you hit diminishing returns. The real learning happens when you encounter those primed words and patterns in real content.","zh":"短时间、专注的预备学习最有效。学习 10～20 分钟词汇就足够了——时间再长，收益就会逐渐递减。真正的学习发生在你于真实内容中遇到那些提前学过的词语和模式时。"}},{"id":"interactive-immersion","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Interactive Immersion","zh":"互动式沉浸"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Interactive immersion is any activity where you're engaging with real content in the target language and actively working to understand it. \"Interactive\" means you're stopping, pausing, looking things up, puzzling through sentences, and generally putting in effort to decode the language.","zh":"互动式沉浸是指接触目标语言的真实内容，并主动努力理解它的任何活动。“互动式”意味着你会停下来、暂停、查找资料、琢磨句子，并整体投入精力来解读这门语言。"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Examples: watching a TV show with subtitles and pausing to look up words, sentence mining, intensive listening (replaying sections to understand), reading with a dictionary, interactive reading with audio.</strong>","zh":"<strong>示例：观看带字幕的电视节目并暂停查词、句子挖掘、精听（反复播放片段以理解内容）、借助词典阅读、带音频的互动式阅读。</strong>"}},{"id":"segment-0010","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<a href=\"https://refold.la/learning-libraries?libraryType=activities&amp;pillar=Interactive\">-&gt; See tutorials for all Interactive activities</a>","zh":"<a href=\"https://refold.la/learning-libraries?libraryType=activities&amp;pillar=Interactive\">-&gt; 查看所有互动式活动的教程</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This is where the bulk of your learning happens. Interactive immersion is the bridge between priming (knowing a word exists) and acquisition (understanding it automatically). It's mentally demanding — if you're not getting a little tired, you're probably not doing it hard enough.","zh":"你的大部分学习都发生在这里。互动式沉浸是预备学习（知道某个词存在）与语言习得（自动理解它）之间的桥梁。它需要大量脑力——如果你一点儿也不觉得累，可能说明练习强度还不够。"}},{"id":"freeflow-immersion","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Freeflow Immersion","zh":"自由流沉浸"}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Freeflow immersion is engaging with content without stopping, looking things up, or actively working to decode. You just let the language flow and focus on the content itself — the story, the information, the entertainment.","zh":"自由流沉浸是指接触内容时不停下来、不查资料，也不主动努力解读。你只需让语言自然流动，并专注于内容本身——故事、信息或娱乐体验。"}},{"id":"segment-0014","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Examples: watching a TV show, listening to a podcast, reading a book.</strong>","zh":"<strong>示例：观看电视节目、收听播客、阅读书籍。</strong>"}},{"id":"segment-0015","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<a href=\"https://refold.la/learning-libraries?libraryType=activities&amp;pillar=Freeflow\">-&gt; See tutorials for all Freeflow activities</a>","zh":"<a href=\"https://refold.la/learning-libraries?libraryType=activities&amp;pillar=Freeflow\">-&gt; 查看所有自由流活动的教程</a>"}},{"id":"segment-0016","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Freeflow builds automaticity. It trains your brain to process the language at natural speed, without the crutch of pausing and translating. It also builds stamina and makes the language feel normal rather than like a study exercise.","zh":"自由流沉浸能够培养自动化能力。它训练大脑以自然速度处理语言，而不再依赖暂停和翻译。它也能增强耐力，让这门语言感觉自然，而不再像一项学习练习。"}},{"id":"segment-0017","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"At low levels, freeflow can feel frustrating because you don't understand much. That's why we recommend starting freeflow with familiar content — things you've already gone through interactively. As your level improves, freeflow becomes the most enjoyable and relaxing part of your routine.","zh":"在水平较低时，自由流沉浸可能令人沮丧，因为你能理解的内容不多。因此，我们建议从熟悉的内容开始自由流沉浸——也就是你已经通过互动方式学习过的内容。随着水平提高，自由流沉浸会成为日常学习中最愉快、最放松的部分。"}},{"id":"output","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Output","zh":"输出"}},{"id":"segment-0019","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Starting in Phase 4, a fourth category enters your routine: <strong>Output</strong>.","zh":"从阶段 4 开始，你的日常学习中会加入第四类活动：<strong>输出</strong>。"}},{"id":"segment-0020","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"This includes speaking (conversation, monologuing, reading aloud) and writing (assisted, unassisted, topic writing).","zh":"这包括口语（对话、独白、朗读）和写作（辅助写作、独立写作、主题写作）。"}},{"id":"segment-0021","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Output isn't technically a \"pillar\" of immersion learning — it's a separate skill that builds on top of your immersion foundation — but it becomes an important part of your daily routine in later phases.","zh":"严格来说，输出并不是沉浸学习的一根“支柱”——它是一项建立在沉浸基础之上的独立技能——但在后期阶段，它会成为日常学习的重要组成部分。"}},{"id":"how-the-balance-shifts","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"How the Balance Shifts","zh":"各项比重如何变化"}},{"id":"segment-0023","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The proportion of time you spend on each pillar changes as you progress:","zh":"随着不断进步，你在每根支柱上投入的时间比例也会发生变化："}},{"id":"segment-0024","type":"table","rows":[[{"en":"Phase","zh":"阶段","header":true},{"en":"Priming","zh":"预备学习","header":true},{"en":"Interactive","zh":"互动式沉浸","header":true},{"en":"Freeflow","zh":"自由流沉浸","header":true},{"en":"Output","zh":"输出","header":true}],[{"en":"Phase 1","zh":"阶段 1","header":false},{"en":"30-50%","zh":"30-50%","header":false},{"en":"50-70%","zh":"50-70%","header":false},{"en":"0-25%","zh":"0-25%","header":false},{"en":"—","zh":"—","header":false}],[{"en":"Phase 2","zh":"阶段 2","header":false},{"en":"20-25%","zh":"20-25%","header":false},{"en":"40-50%","zh":"40-50%","header":false},{"en":"25-40%","zh":"25-40%","header":false},{"en":"—","zh":"—","header":false}],[{"en":"Phase 3","zh":"阶段 3","header":false},{"en":"10-20%","zh":"10-20%","header":false},{"en":"40-60%","zh":"40-60%","header":false},{"en":"20-50%","zh":"20-50%","header":false},{"en":"—","zh":"—","header":false}],[{"en":"Phase 4","zh":"阶段 4","header":false},{"en":"10%","zh":"10%","header":false},{"en":"20-30%","zh":"20-30%","header":false},{"en":"30-40%","zh":"30-40%","header":false},{"en":"20-40%","zh":"20-40%","header":false}],[{"en":"Phase 5","zh":"阶段 5","header":false},{"en":"10-15%","zh":"10-15%","header":false},{"en":"20-30%","zh":"20-30%","header":false},{"en":"20-30%","zh":"20-30%","header":false},{"en":"30-50%","zh":"30-50%","header":false}],[{"en":"Phase 6+","zh":"阶段 6+","header":false},{"en":"10-15%","zh":"10-15%","header":false},{"en":"10-30%","zh":"10-30%","header":false},{"en":"20-50%","zh":"20-50%","header":false},{"en":"20-40%","zh":"20-40%","header":false}]]},{"id":"segment-0025","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>The general trend</strong>: priming decreases over time as you need less explicit study, interactive stays important throughout, freeflow grows as your comprehension improves, and output enters in Phase 4 and grows from there.","zh":"<strong>总体趋势</strong>：随着你越来越不需要显性学习，预备学习会逐渐减少；互动式沉浸始终重要；随着理解能力提高，自由流沉浸会逐渐增加；输出则从阶段 4 开始加入，并在此后逐步增加。"}},{"id":"segment-0026","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<em>Note: This is a rough guideline, not a hard and fast rule.</em>","zh":"<em>注意：这只是大致的指导原则，并非硬性规定。</em>"}},{"id":"the-key-principle","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"The Key Principle","zh":"核心原则"}},{"id":"segment-0028","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>No single pillar is enough.</strong>","zh":"<strong>任何一根支柱都无法独自发挥足够作用。</strong>"}},{"id":"segment-0029","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Priming without immersion gives you a list of words you can't use. Interactive immersion without priming is painfully slow because you're looking up everything from scratch. Freeflow without interactive gives you vague familiarity without real understanding.","zh":"只有预备学习而没有沉浸，你得到的只会是一份不会使用的词汇表。只有互动式沉浸而没有预备学习，进度会慢得令人痛苦，因为一切都要从头查起。只有自由流沉浸而没有互动式沉浸，你只会产生模糊的熟悉感，而无法真正理解。"}},{"id":"segment-0030","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"All three work together to build strong abilities from nothing.","zh":"三者相辅相成，帮助你从零开始培养扎实的语言能力。"}},{"id":"research-and-reasoning","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Research and Reasoning","zh":"研究与理论依据"}},{"id":"segment-0032","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The three-pillar framework draws on decades of second language acquisition research. The role of comprehensible input as the foundation for acquisition is well-established in Krashen's (1982) Input Hypothesis and remains central to modern SLA despite ongoing theoretical debates.","zh":"三支柱框架借鉴了数十年来的第二语言习得研究。可理解输入作为语言习得基础的作用，早已在 Krashen（1982）的输入假说中得到确立；尽管理论争论仍在继续，它至今仍是现代第二语言习得研究的核心。"}},{"id":"segment-0033","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The distinction between receptive knowledge (understanding) and productive knowledge (using language) is grounded in the research on implicit versus explicit learning. Schmidt (1990) demonstrated that explicit focus on form helps learners notice patterns in input, which supports the priming pillar's approach. However, research by Ellis (2015) and others shows that form-focused instruction is most effective when integrated with meaning-focused activity — exactly the model described here.","zh":"接受性知识（理解语言）与产出性知识（使用语言）之间的区别，建立在内隐学习与显性学习的相关研究之上。Schmidt（1990）证明，明确关注语言形式有助于学习者注意到输入中的模式，这为预备学习支柱所采用的方法提供了支持。然而，Ellis（2015）等人的研究表明，语言形式教学与以意义为中心的活动相结合时效果最佳——这正是本文所描述的模式。"}},{"id":"segment-0034","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The emphasis on gradually reducing priming and increasing freeflow aligns with skill acquisition theory (DeKeyser, 2015), which describes how language moves from controlled, conscious processing (interactive immersion with pausing) to automatic, unconscious processing (freeflow). Building automaticity through massive amounts of exposure is essential for reaching fluency that feels natural and effortless.","zh":"逐渐减少预备学习并增加自由流沉浸的做法，符合技能习得理论（DeKeyser，2015）。该理论描述了语言处理如何从受控、有意识的处理（会暂停的互动式沉浸）转变为自动、无意识的处理（自由流沉浸）。通过大量接触培养自动化能力，是达到自然且毫不费力的流利程度所不可或缺的。"}}],"cards":[]}}]
